# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: relational-operators-ignore-strings — (< "a" "b") returns nil in clautolisp
#+STATUS: DONE (clautolisp 2.2.87 / alfe 2.2.82, 2026-09-24)
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: claude/dreamy-ptolemy-uj8mzd

* Symptom

Reported by pjb on PF5S26BT (same output in every dialect: strict,
clautolisp, bricscad, autocad, lax; and through =alfe --cad clautolisp=):

| expression                                  | clautolisp    | BricsCAD V25 / AutoCAD 2022 |
|---------------------------------------------+---------------+-----------------------------|
| =(list (< "a" "b") (= "a" "b") (> "a" "b"))= | =(nil nil nil)= | =(T nil nil)=               |
| =(list (< "b" "b") (= "b" "b") (> "b" "b"))= | =(nil T nil)=   | =(nil T nil)=               |
| =(list (< "c" "b") (= "c" "b") (> "c" "b"))= | =(nil nil nil)= | =(nil nil T)=               |

=== was right; =<=, =<==, =>=, =>== never compared strings.

* Cause

=numeric-order-p= (=autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp=) folded ANY
non-number to nil — the rule kept for the =(<= 48 (car chars) 57)=
loop-guard idiom (strict-dialect-autolisp-divergences §2) — so strings,
which the spec (ch.5, Function Entry: =<=) orders lexicographically by code
point, fell into the same fold.

* Resolution (clautolisp 2.2.87)

All-string argument lists are now compared pairwise with =string<= /
=string<== / =string>= / =string>== (code-point order, case-sensitive); a
nil still folds the comparison to nil. Dialect classification: case 0
(common — both reference documents and both products agree), so no
warning. Regression test =relational-operators-order-strings=
(=autolisp-builtins-core/tests/builtin-tests.lisp=); string cases added to
the compiler's open-coded corpus (the integer fast path declines strings,
so compiled and interpreted code agree).

The remaining gap — a number/string mixture folds to nil where the spec
says type error — is tracked separately by
=issues/open/relational-cross-type-arguments-should-signal.issue=.
